### Step 4 – Drilldown and hierarchies

#### What I did in Power BI
- Created new page: `3.1.4 – Drilldown`.
- Created three hierarchies in the model:
  - `Date Hierarchy`: Year → Month → Date (in dim_date).
  - `Store Hierarchy`: Region → StoreName (in dim_store).
  - `Product Hierarchy`: Category → Subcategory → ProductName (in dim_product).
- Built a **column chart** with `Date Hierarchy` on Axis and `[Total Sales]` on Values:
  - Used drill buttons to:
    - Drill down from Year → Month → Date.
    - Drill up back to Year.
    - Use "Go to next level" and "Expand all down one level".
- Built a **bar/column chart** with `Store Hierarchy`:
  - Started at Region level and drilled down to individual stores.
- Built a **matrix** with `Product Hierarchy` on Rows and `[Total Sales]` on Values:
  - Used the +/- icons to expand and collapse Category → Subcategory → ProductName.

#### What I learned
- Hierarchies group multiple levels (Year, Month, Date) into a single field, making drilldown easy.
- Drilldown changes the level of detail in a visual without changing the measure.
- "Drill down" focuses on the selected item; "Go to next level" shows all items at the next level.
- "Expand all down one level" shows multiple hierarchy levels at the same time (e.g. all Years with their Months).
- Matrices use +/- icons for drilldown through row hierarchies.
